      <div>
        <p class="profile-detail-region">Battle · South &amp; Southeast Asia</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Third Battle of Panipat</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">14 January 1761, after skirmishing and a siege of about two months</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">In and around the city of Panipat, about 97 kilometres (60 mi) north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a>, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha Empire</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sadashivrao-bhau">Sadashivrao Bhau</a>, with an army put at between 45,000 and 60,000 and roughly 200,000 non-combatants; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durrani-empire">Durrani Empire</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-shah-abdali">Ahmad Shah Durrani</a> (Abdali), with Najib-ud-Daula, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rohillas">Rohillas</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shuja-ud-daula">Shuja-ud-Daula</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/awadh">Oudh</a>. Over 125,000 troops are given for the whole battle.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Afghan army won after several <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> flanks were destroyed. Between 60,000 and 70,000 troops are believed to have been killed in the fighting, and about 40,000 Maratha prisoners were killed the next day according to an eyewitness chronicle.</span></div>
        </div>
